\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces One factorized coarse correction, from $r$ (left) to $e$ (right), on its three lattices (the Pauli--Villars coarse solve in orange, the quark one in green): $u=\mathcal  P(\mathcal  P^{\dagger }D_{\mathrm  {PV}}^{\dagger }\mathcal  P)^{-1}\mathcal  P^{\dagger }\iota O_Rr$ is the result of the first coarse solve, its even part times $O_M$ is the right-hand side of the second, whose result is $v=\mathcal  P\mathcal  D_{\mathrm  c}^{-1}\mathcal  P^{\dagger }\iota O_M\pi u$, and $e=O_L\pi v$. In blue, after ``$=$'', the values for $r=\tilde  A_{R}y$ in the right form with exact coarse solves and $s,\hat  t\in \operatorname  {range}\mathcal  P$ (Sec.~\ref {sec:exact}; $O_R=C_{\mathrm  {PV},e}^{\dagger }$, $O_M=1$, $O_L=C_{e}$): the first solve returns the lift $\hat  t$, whose even part is $a=\pi Ds$, the second returns the lift $s$, and the correction returns $y$.}}{11}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:correction}{{1}{11}{One factorized coarse correction, from $r$ (left) to $e$ (right), on its three lattices (the Pauli--Villars coarse solve in orange, the quark one in green): $u=\Pro (\Pro \dg \Dpv \dg \Pro )^{-1}\Pro \dg \iota O_Rr$ is the result of the first coarse solve, its even part times $O_M$ is the right-hand side of the second, whose result is $v=\Pro \Dc ^{-1}\Pro \dg \iota O_M\pi u$, and $e=O_L\pi v$. In blue, after ``$=$'', the values for $r=\AR y$ in the right form with exact coarse solves and $s,\hat t\in \operatorname {range}\Pro $ (Sec.~\ref {sec:exact}; $O_R=\Cpve \dg $, $O_M=1$, $O_L=\Ce $): the first solve returns the lift $\hat t$, whose even part is $a=\pi Ds$, the second returns the lift $s$, and the correction returns $y$}{figure.1}{}}
